## Increment 2 of the concurrency adoption (§4.1 piece 2 — state-indexed
## drop glue). An `async def` lowers to a Future STATE MACHINE that owns its
## awaited sub-future as a `self.__sub_0` field. When that state-machine
## future is DRAINED while parked at suspend #0, the sub-future is still
## live — its `def drop` MUST fire. Increment 1 made the drain reach the
## state machine's `def drop` via Drop_dynamic_drop; Increment 2 synthesises
## that `def drop` to actually drop the live `__sub_0` field (Ruxen has no
## automatic per-field drop, so the synthesised drop must do it explicitly).
##
## Pre-Increment-2 the state machine got the `_drop_noop` (Increment 1) —
## draining it ran a no-op and `PendingForever_drop` NEVER fired (the
## sub-future's reactor/fd analogue leaked). The sentinel below proves the
## sub-future's drop now runs on drain.
##
## Shape: `handler` awaits a `PendingForever` sub-future that never
## completes. main spawns handler(), pumps once (sub_0 constructed + polled
## → Pending, so the state machine parks at __state == 0), then drains.
## Drain → __HandlerFuture_drop → drops self.__sub_0 → PendingForever_drop.

class PendingForever
  payload: Int
  include Future
  type Output = Int

  def init(p: Int)
    self.payload = p
  end

  def self.make(p: Int) -> PendingForever
    PendingForever.new(p)
  end

  def var poll(cx: &var Context) -> Poll[Int]
    # Never completes — exists only to be parked then dropped on drain.
    Poll.Pending
  end

  def drop
    puts "PendingForever dropped payload=#{self.payload}"
  end
end

## State machine: __sub_0 = PendingForever (eagerly constructed in init),
## parked at __state == 0 after the first Pending poll.
async def handler() -> Int
  let v = PendingForever.make(99).await
  v
end

def main
  let h = Task.spawn_raw(handler())
  # Pump once: the spawned __HandlerFuture polls, constructs+polls __sub_0
  # (Pending), and stays queued at __state == 0.
  let _pumped = ruxen_executor_pump_tasks()
  puts "parked"
  # Drain the still-parked state-machine future. Its def drop must drop the
  # live __sub_0, firing PendingForever_drop exactly once.
  ruxen_executor_drain_remaining()
  puts "drained"
end
